{"cuisine/ivorian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/ivorian-cuisine","n":"Ivorian cuisine","c":"#e46a3f","crumb":[["Africa","cuisines#africa"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Côte d'Ivoire","intro":[["Ivorian cuisine is the traditional cuisine of Côte d'Ivoire, and is based on tubers, grains, pig, chicken, seafood, fish, fresh fruits, vegetables and spices. It is very similar to that of neighboring countries in West Africa. Common staple foods include grains and tubers. Côte d'Ivoire is one of the largest cocoa producers in the world and also produces palm oil and coffee."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ivorian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivorian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]}],"cont":"African cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/b/b7/Cuisine_of_Ivory_Coast_%28158425691%29.jpg/500px-Cuisine_of_Ivory_Coast_%28158425691%29.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Louis Massuel","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cuisine_of_Ivory_Coast_(158425691).jpg"}},"ingredient/filo":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/filo","n":"Filo","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 3 dishes across 6 cuisines","intro":[["Filo or yufka (Turkish: [jufˈka]) is a very thin unleavened pastry dough used for making baked goods. Filo-based products are made by layering many sheets of filo brushed with oil or butter; the pastry is then baked."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-filo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":6,"groups":[["Austrian cuisine","cuisine/austrian-cuisine",[["Strudel","dish/strudel"]]],["Bulgarian cuisine","cuisine/bulgarian-cuisine",[["Banitsa","dish/banitsa"]]],["Czech cuisine","cuisine/czech-cuisine",[["Strudel","dish/strudel"]]],["German cuis